                  {
                    "value": "7 \u00b7 Terminal Value \u2014 from scratch",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "13pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "After year 5 the business keeps producing cash forever, growing at g. Discount that infinite stream one year at a time: TV = CF\u2086/(1+r) + CF\u2086(1+g)/(1+r)\u00b2 + CF\u2086(1+g)\u00b2/(1+r)\u00b3 + \u2026",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Each term is the previous one \u00d7 (1+g)/(1+r) \u2014 a geometric series with ratio < 1, so the infinite sum collapses to a finite number: TV = CF\u2086 \u00f7 (r \u2212 g) = CF\u2085 \u00d7 (1+g) \u00f7 (r \u2212 g).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "= 235.1 \u00d7 1.025 \u00f7 (0.0911 \u2212 0.025) = 241.0 \u00f7 0.0661 = $3.645B as of year 5, then discounted 5 years home: 3,645 \u00f7 1.546 = $2.36B. g = 2.5% is a stated ASSUMPTION (must sit below long-run GDP growth).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "\u2192 tab 6 \u00b7 Valuation & Recommendation",
